From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - select parts of the tool, not parts of
 the cut result, in BRepFeat_MakeCylindricalHole

The four BRepFeat_MakeCylindricalHole modes that choose which piece of the
drilling tool to keep -- PerformThruNext, PerformUntilEnd, the ranged
Perform(Radius, PFrom, PTo) and PerformBlind -- all drive BRepFeat_Builder with
the wrong operation:

    SetOperation(Fuse);        // -> BOPAlgo_CUT
    BOPAlgo_BOP::Perform();    // myShape := object CUT tool
    PartsOfTool(parts);        // explores myShape for solids
    ... KeepPart(chosen) ...

BRepFeat_Builder::PartsOfTool() collects the solids of myShape, which is only
the tool split by the object after the COMMON pass. After a CUT it is the cut
result, so the selection loops compare barycentres of the finished workpiece and
then register those pieces as "kept parts of the tool". PerformResult() takes
the kept-parts path with a keep set containing no tool part at all, and returns
the object with the cylinder's faces imprinted on it and no material removed --
reporting BRepFeat_NoError throughout.

The other two users of the same builder already do this correctly:
BRepFeat_Form (BRepFeat_Form.cxx:806) and BRepFeat_RibSlot
(BRepFeat_RibSlot.cxx:224) both call the two-argument
SetOperation(myFuse, bFlag) with bFlag true before Perform(), so that
PartsOfTool() means what its name says. PerformResult() resets myOperation from
myFuse, so the operation finally built is still the CUT either way.

The defect is invisible whenever the cut result happens to have one solid, which
is the single-plate case every existing test uses. It shows up as soon as it has
two: a drill axis crossing two bodies of a compound, or -- with no compound
involved -- a single bar the bore severs in half.

Measured on a compound of two 50x50x20 plates stacked on the drill axis (plate A
at axis parameters 5..25, plate B at 45..65), drilled at r = 5 from (0, 0, 15)
along -Z. One plate's bore removes 1570.7963:

    call                     status   before      after
    Perform(R)               NoError  3141.5927   3141.5927   (unaffected)
    PerformUntilEnd          NoError     0.0000   3141.5927
    PerformThruNext          NoError  1570.7963   1570.7963
    PerformBlind(20)         NoError     0.0000   1178.0972
    Perform(R, 0, 70)        NoError     0.0000   3141.5927
    Perform(R, 0, 30)        NoError  1570.7963   1570.7963
    Perform(R, 30, 70)       NoError  1570.7963   1570.7963

and on a single 8mm-wide bar that a r = 5 bore severs, where "parts" was two
pieces of one workpiece rather than two bodies:

    PerformUntilEnd          NoError     0.0000   1407.2952
    PerformThruNext          NoError     0.0000   1407.2952
    Perform(R, 0, 30)        NoError     0.0000   1407.2952

Perform(Radius) selects no parts and is left on the one-argument overload.

One further behaviour change follows from the fix, on a radius so large the bore
swallows the whole workpiece: under CUT that emptied myShape, so nbparts was 0
and the mode returned BRepFeat_InvalidPlacement. Under COMMON the tool meets the
whole workpiece, nbparts is 1, and the modes now return the empty result that
Perform(Radius) and a plain BRepAlgoAPI_Cut against the same cylinder already
returned. nbparts == 0 now means what the guard reads as: the tool meets nothing.
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFeat/BRepFeat/BRepFeat_MakeCylindricalHole.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFeat/BRepFeat/BRepFeat_MakeCylindricalHole.cxx
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@
 
   bool Fuse = false;
   AddTool(theTool);
-  SetOperation(Fuse);
+  SetOperation(Fuse, true); // split the tool, so PartsOfTool() below has parts to select
   BOPAlgo_BOP::Perform();
   NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape> parts;
   PartsOfTool(parts);
@@ -318,7 +318,7 @@
 
   bool Fuse = false;
   AddTool(theTool);
-  SetOperation(Fuse);
+  SetOperation(Fuse, true); // split the tool, so PartsOfTool() below has parts to select
   BOPAlgo_BOP::Perform();
   NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape> parts;
   PartsOfTool(parts);
@@ -434,7 +434,7 @@
 
   bool Fuse = false;
   AddTool(theTool);
-  SetOperation(Fuse);
+  SetOperation(Fuse, true); // split the tool, so PartsOfTool() below has parts to select
   BOPAlgo_BOP::Perform();
   NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape> parts;
   PartsOfTool(parts);
@@ -566,7 +566,7 @@
   // myBuilder.Perform(theTool,theList,Fuse);
   // myBuilder.BuildPartsOfTool();
   AddTool(theTool);
-  SetOperation(Fuse);
+  SetOperation(Fuse, true); // split the tool, so PartsOfTool() below has parts to select
   BOPAlgo_BOP::Perform();
   NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape> parts;
   PartsOfTool(parts);
